[{:db/id -1 :doc/id "business-openrouter-provider-blockers-20260908" :doc/title "OpenRouter application blockers after fleet verification" :doc/as-of "2026-09-08" :source/dataset "business" :doc/body "# Application blockers after fleet sustained and cancellation checks\n\n2026-09-08. Primary: Murakumo fleet. Modal: matching-model stability backup only, with recovery-driven failback. Submission status remains not submitted; candidate is_ready remains false.\n\n## Closed or materially advanced\nAPI #241 merged bfe6f72c169c08aff6ea62046999162f206406ea; root pin 9f5215db877a743fbdd848fe3b2a38cfbc1ca535; deployed c1bd9bf9-66b2-458a-8873-81d31814c19e. The Worker now watches downstream writer closure and aborts upstream prefill without waiting for the next 15-second heartbeat. Built-artifact regression: old version fails specifically because origin abort is absent, new version passes while Request.signal remains un-aborted. Eight cancellation/admission/proxy tests, 25 catalog tests with 107 assertions and three native tests pass. The catalog now includes the verified upstream hugging_face_id Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B, observed live after deployment.\n\nBounded continuous public run, 08:37:46.288-08:42:39.762 UTC: 20 sequential pairs at 15-second cadence, 40/40 success, no 429, p95 elapsed 7090 ms, maximum 8278 ms. Actual duration 293.474 seconds. This is about five minutes of short prompts, not a peak-capacity benchmark or seven-day history. Load requests are in a separate ledger, not inserted into the normal soak ledger. SHA256 9f60a0b0c994e4df0373aa61a30f50d80344a27582d8be378de2bd497ae58669.\n\nLive cancellation at 08:44:58.318 UTC: first content was observed without DONE; the origin slot was busy; only the response body was cancelled, with the caller Request signal still not aborted. The slot became idle by 4168 ms after cancellation. Origin journal independently recorded cancel task id 56012 and release of that same task at n_tokens=259. This proves origin cancellation for this observed midstream request, not an instantaneous universal latency bound or restart recovery. Before-first-token cancellation is covered by the built-worker regression; a repeated live cold-prefill campaign is still unmeasured.\n\n## Remaining release/submission blockers\n1. Reliability and backup: finish long-duration observation, sustained parallel and long-context load, controlled backend stop/restart recovery, matching-model Modal failure routing, cooldown and failback. Existing Modal GLM-5.3-Flash does not substitute for Qwen3.8-27B. Verify a compatible backup and spend ceiling before activation. Separate fleet success from backup-rescued success; never recurse through OpenRouter. Owner's backup architecture is a product acceptance requirement, not a published OpenRouter mandate.\n2. Partner authorization and settlement: issue scoped partner credentials; establish durable, idempotent request/attempt attribution, complete streaming usage, cancellation/unknown treatment, atomic credit/reservation accounting and reconciliation to actual vendor and customer invoices. Offline #240 reconciliation is an aid, not deployed billing. Budget-estimate records are not actual invoices.\n3. Retention and public disclosures: final terms/privacy, actual Cloudflare logging, R2/Merkle history and deletion/compaction, accounting metadata and conditional Modal processing. The 4/4 source checks verify narrow current disclosures; they do not prove physical erasure or whole-service ZDR. Current draft legal pages are not a final partner data contract.\n4. Commercial identity and rights: verified contracting entity, jurisdiction/filing/address and billing contact; payment mechanism with OpenRouter (auto top-up or invoicing); applicable Modal terms or written permission for the backup resale scope. Do not equate a public company name with registration evidence. Modal account access and the actual Service Order remain unavailable in this session. No vendor clarification sent.\n5. Unit economics and capacity: fleet cost per useful completed output plus measured backup incidence/cost, retries, idle capacity and edge fees; then set and validate offer price and sustainable capacity. Published Modal prices alone neither establish fleet cost nor prove a fleet offer is loss-making.\n\n## Timing versus hard eligibility\nSeven days / >=1000 non-429 samples / >=500 per mode / >=99.5% correctness / <=45-minute gaps are OUR internal low-volume qualification policy, not an OpenRouter-stated universal application waiting period. Earliest seven-day age remains 2026-09-15T05:39:47.525Z if coverage and counts pass. Do not claim readiness merely when the calendar reaches that time. About three hours of current observation cannot establish seven days.\nThe official provider requirements cover model catalog/identity, capabilities/prices/capacity and payment integration, among other operational fields. The catalog shape and upstream identity are now evidenced; partner settlement and truthful operational/commercial claims remain unresolved. An exploratory contact can describe these gaps, but is not an accepted production provider.\n\nPrimary source: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/community/for-providers\n"}]
